        "content": {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "\\nGuidelines:\\n\`\`\`\\nroot_access: list_roots lists configured or accepted roots; every other tool is scoped to them.\\nmodern_root_grants: Modern clients do not automatically send workspace roots. Call a tool with a concrete path and approve its grant when elicitation is available.\\npath_resolution: Confirm a path with list or find_files before acting on it.\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nTools Overview:\\n\`\`\`\\nNavigate: list_roots, list, find_files\\nInspect: stat, search_text\\nRead: read\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nFull schemas, descriptions, and annotations are in \`tools/list\`.\\n\\nConstraints:\\n\`\`\`\\nallowed_roots: Startup roots come from CLI paths, FS_ALLOWED_DIRS, or --allow-cwd; accepted modern grants are additive. Call list_roots to read the current set.\\nlegacy_roots: Legacy clients may additionally seed roots through the deprecated roots/list flow.\\nsensitive_paths: Sensitive file paths (.env, *.pem, SSH private keys such as *id_rsa* and *id_ed25519*, .netrc, .git-credentials) are denied by default.\\nenforced_limits: max file size 10 MiB (also the combined content cap of one create call), stdio responses up to 9.8 MiB once JSON-encoded (HTTP has no such limit), file search cap 10000 results, content search scans up to 10000 matches, paged by maxResults (default 500).\\nephemeral_results: When a result carries a resource_link or a resourceUri (in structuredContent or _meta), call resources/read immediately — cached results are ephemeral and expire after ~60 seconds, eviction, or restart.\\npagination: nextCursor appears in the result text and in _meta, backed by a snapshot on the same ~60s clock. Send the printed Next page call as-is (the original arguments plus cursor); if a cursor is rejected, start again without one. resourceUri appears on the first page only.\\n\`\`\`\\n\\nError Recovery:\\n\`\`\`\\nACCESS_DENIED: Run list_roots; configure a missing startup root or retry a concrete path and approve the grant.\\nNOT_FOUND: Run list or find_files to verify the path.\\nTOO_LARGE: Over the file size limit, use read with head/tail or startLine/endLine. Over the stdio message limit, request a smaller slice or page, or connect over HTTP; media and binary files need HTTP.\\nTIMEOUT: Narrow path or pattern, or lower maxDepth; maxResults only sizes a page.\\nINVALID_INPUT: Re-read the tool schema in tools/list.\\nBINARY_FILE: Text tools refuse binary files; read returns one whole with binary: true.\\n\`\`\`\\n",
          "annotations": {
            "audience": [
              "assistant"
            ],
            "priority": 1
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}
`;
